Rāma addresses waiting Lakṣmaṇa with folded hands --- Rāma asks who will support Kausalyā and Sumitrā if both follow --- Rāma warns love-bound king cannot guard and Kaikēyī will neglect co-wives --- Lakṣmaṇa answers Bharata will honor both mothers by Rāma glory --- Lakṣmaṇa notes Kausalyā feeds a thousand through thousand villages --- Lakṣmaṇa vows to lead with spade basket bow showing the path --- Lakṣmaṇa vows to fetch roots fruits guard sleeping Rāma with Sītā --- Rāma bids take leave of kin, fetch Varuṇa bows armor quivers swords --- Lakṣmaṇa greets preceptor and displays garlanded divine arms --- Rāma bids distribute wealth with him and fetch noble Suyajña
